.TH WOCHE 1 "October 2026" "woche 1.6.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
woche \- weekly task manager for the command line
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B woche
.I command
.RI [ arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B woche
keeps one Markdown file per week, named after the week's Monday
.RI ( YYMMDD.md ),
with a section per day:
.PP
.RS
.nf
# Monday, 28/9
\- open task
\- [x] finished task
.fi
.RE
.PP
The files are plain Markdown: they can be edited by hand, synced or kept in git.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B create
Create the file for the current week.
.TP
.BI "mon " "\(dqtask\(dq"
Add a task to the end of a day.
Days: mon, tue, wed, thu, fri, sat, sun (German: mont, die, mit, don, fre, sam, son).
.TP
.BI "today " "\(dqtask\(dq"
Add a task to the current day.
.TP
.BR show " [" last | \fIYYMMDD\fR]
Show the tasks of the current, last or given week.
Each task gets an address such as
.BR mon.2 ,
the second task on Monday.
.TP
.BI "done " "day n"
Mark a task as finished.
.TP
.BI "edit " "day n \(dqnew text\(dq"
Change the text of a task. A finished task stays finished.
.TP
.BI "delete " "day n"
Delete a task, after confirmation.
.TP
.BI "search " "\(dqtext\(dq"
Search all weeks for a literal text.
.TP
.B all
List the weekly files.
.TP
.B open
Open the current week in
.BR $EDITOR .
.TP
.B init
Choose the language and the directory of the weekly files.
Runs by itself the first time woche is used in a terminal.
.TP
.B config
Show the configuration.
.TP
.BR "config language " en | de
Language of the day names in new weeks.
.TP
.BI "config dir " path
Directory of the weekly files. Existing files are not moved.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show the version.
.PP
Tasks can also be addressed as
.B mon.2
or by the line number in the file, as in older versions.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B WOCHE_DIR
Directory of the weekly files (overrides the config file). Default:
.IR ~/woche .
.TP
.B WOCHE_LANGUAGE
.BR en " or " de
(overrides the config file).
.TP
.B WOCHE_WEEK
Work on another week, given as its Monday in
.I YYMMDD
format, e.g. to fill in last week.
.TP
.B EDITOR
Editor used by
.BR open .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.woche/config
Shell-style settings:
.B WOCHE_LANGUAGE
and
.BR WOCHE_DIR .
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
woche create
woche mon "Team meeting at 10am"
woche show
woche done mon 1
WOCHE_WEEK=260921 woche fri "Filled in later"
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
https://github.com/0jonjo/woche
